n: 4 System architecture" class=3D"mw-editsection-visualeditor"><span>edit<=
/span></a><span class=3D"mw-editsection-divider"> | </span><a href=3D"https=
://wiki.itxpt.org/w/index.php?title=3DS03P01-_TiGR_-_v3.0.3&amp;action=3Ded=
it&amp;section=3D4" title=3D"Edit section's source code: 4 System architect=
ure"><span>edit source</span></a><span class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">]</=
span></span></h2>
<ul><li>Telediagnostic system architecture consists of:
<ul><li>An <b>On-Board Unit</b> (OBU) provided by a third party (VehMan or =
ITS supplier) for each vehicle monitored;</li>
<li>Different <b>FM back-offices</b> collecting data from the OBUs (one for=
 each OBU supplier);</li>
<li><b>A connector from each FM back-office to Telediagnostic back-office</=
b>, consisting of a RESTful Web Service Client implemented in the FM back-o=
ffice and a Server provided by Telediagnostic back-office;</li>
<li><b>Telediagnostic back-office</b> integrating data from different back-=
office interfaces.</li></ul></li></ul>
<p><span typeof=3D"mw:File"><span><img src=3D"https://wiki.itxpt.org/w/imag=
es/thumb/a/ac/S03v2_2017_Fig6.png/800px-S03v2_2017_Fig6.png" decoding=3D"as=
ync" width=3D"800" height=3D"398" class=3D"mw-file-element"></span></span><=
br>
<i><b>Figure 1- Telediagnostic system architecture</b></i>
</p>
<ul><li>Events structure:
<ul><li>The transfer of data in the connector between FM back-offices and T=
elediagnostic server shall be event driven (Periodic and OnChange).</li></u=
l></li></ul>
<h3><span class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"4.1_Event_Header">4.1 Event Header</s=
pan><span class=3D"mw-editsection"><span class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">[=
</span><a href=3D"https://wiki.itxpt.org/w/index.php?title=3DS03P01-_TiGR_-=
_v3.0.3&amp;veaction=3Dedit&amp;section=3D5" title=3D"Edit section: 4.1 Eve=
nt Header" class=3D"mw-editsection-visualeditor"><span>edit</span></a><span=
 class=3D"mw-editsection-divider"> | </span><a href=3D"https://wiki.itxpt.o=
rg/w/index.php?title=3DS03P01-_TiGR_-_v3.0.3&amp;action=3Dedit&amp;section=
=3D5" title=3D"Edit section's source code: 4.1 Event Header"><span>edit sou=
rce</span></a><span class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></h3>
<figure class=3D"mw-halign-left" typeof=3D"mw:File/Frameless"><span title=
=3D"Mandatory"><img alt=3D"Mandatory" src=3D"https://wiki.itxpt.org/w/image=
s/e/e3/Mandatory.png" decoding=3D"async" width=3D"35" height=3D"33" class=
=3D"mw-file-element"></span><figcaption>Mandatory</figcaption></figure><p>E=
ach event message (vehicle fault, ITS fault, system diagnostic and manual i=
nput) shall consist of a header with a standard format in accordance with s=
tructure "Header" as defined in 12.2 below.
</p><p>Each event message may contain additional structure(s) with variable=
 list of associated data depending on event type. These additional structur=
es =E2=80=9CEventON=E2=80=9D, =E2=80=9CEventOFF=E2=80=9D, =E2=80=9CEventTRK=
=E2=80=9D, =E2=80=9CEventLT=E2=80=9D and =E2=80=9CEXTRA=E2=80=9D are define=
d in Table 1.
</p><p>The message header shall include the following parameters:=20
</p>
<table class=3D"wikitable" style=3D"background-color:white;" cellpadding=3D=
"5">
<tbody><tr>
<th colspan=3D"4"><b>Header parameters</b>
</th></tr>
<tr>
<th colspan=3D"2"><b>Field</b>
</th>
<th><b>Description</b>
</th>
<th><b>Availability</b>
</th></tr>
<tr>
<td colspan=3D"2">=E2=80=9CID=E2=80=9D
</td>
<td>Data provider Id (assigned by Telediagnostic service supplier)
</td>
<td>[mandatory]
</td></tr>
<tr>
<td colspan=3D"2">=E2=80=9CVERS=E2=80=9D
</td>
<td>Version of implemented TiGR specification release
</td>
<td>[mandatory]
</td></tr>
<tr>
<td colspan=3D"2">=E2=80=9CSERVERNAME=E2=80=9D
</td>
<td>Mnemonic identifier of connector client (to be agreed with  telediagnos=
tic service supplier)
</td>
<td>[mandatory]
</td></tr>
<tr>
<td colspan=3D"2">=E2=80=9CVIN=E2=80=9D
</td>
<td>Vehicle Identification (VIN)
</td>
<td>[mandatory]
</td></tr>
<tr>
<td colspan=3D"2">=E2=80=9CBID=E2=80=9D
</td>
<td>Battery identification  number
</td>
<td>[recommended]
</td></tr>
<tr>
<td colspan=3D"2">=E2=80=9CPROG=E2=80=9D
</td>
<td>Event serial No.
</td>
<td>[mandatory]
</td></tr>
<tr>
<td colspan=3D"2">=E2=80=9CEVTDATE=E2=80=9D
</td>
<td>Event DateTime [UNIX format]
</td>
<td>[mandatory]
</td></tr>
<tr>
<td colspan=3D"2">=E2=80=9CTRSDATE=E2=80=9D
</td>
<td>Event Transmission DateTime [UNIX format]
</td>
<td>[mandatory]
</td></tr>
<tr>
<td colspan=3D"2">=E2=80=9CSRVDATE=E2=80=9D
</td>
<td>Event Server DateTime [UNIX format]
</td>
<td>[mandatory]
</td></tr>
<tr>
<td colspan=3D"2">=E2=80=9CSENDDATE=E2=80=9D
</td>
<td>Event Send DateTime [UNIX format]
</td>
<td>[mandatory]
</td></tr>
<tr>
<td colspan=3D"2">=E2=80=9CTIMEZONE=E2=80=9D
</td>
<td>Offset from Coordinated Universal Time (UTC)
</td>
<td>[recommended]
</td></tr>
<tr>
<td colspan=3D"2">=E2=80=9CCODE=E2=80=9D
</td>
<td>TiGR Event Code as defined in 4.2
</td>
<td>[mandatory]
</td></tr>
<tr>
<td colspan=3D"2">=E2=80=9CTYPE=E2=80=9D
</td>
<td>Structure of additional data to be sent with the event
</td>
<td>[mandatory]
</td></tr>
<tr>
<td colspan=3D"2">=E2=80=9CDST=E2=80=9D
</td>
<td>Vehicle Mileage
</td>
<td>[mandatory]
</td></tr>
<tr>
<td colspan=3D"2">=E2=80=9CGPSInfo=E2=80=9D
</td>
<td>Current GNSS position information
</td>
<td>[mandatory]
</td></tr>
<tr>
<td>
</td>
<td>=E2=80=9CLAT=E2=80=9D
</td>
<td>Latitude of GNSS coordinate
<p>Format is DD*60000 (decimal degrees=E2=80=99 format)
</p>
</td>
<td>[mandatory]
</td></tr>
<tr>
<td>
</td>
<td>=E2=80=9CLON=E2=80=9D
</td>
<td>Longitude of GNSS coordinate
<p>Format is DD*60000 (decimal degrees=E2=80=99 format)
</p>
</td>
<td>[mandatory]
</td></tr>
<tr>
<td>
</td>
<td>=E2=80=9CALT=E2=80=9D
</td>
<td>Altitude of GNSS coordinate
</td>
<td>[mandatory]
</td></tr>
<tr>
<td>
</td>
<td>=E2=80=9CHEAD=E2=80=9D
</td>
<td>Heading of GNSS coordinate
</td>
<td>[recommended]
</td></tr>
<tr>
<td>
</td>
<td>=E2=80=9CNUMSAT=E2=80=9D
</td>
<td>Number of satellites available
</td>
<td>[recommended]
</td></tr>
<tr>
<td>
</td>
<td>=E2=80=9CDOP=E2=80=9D
</td>
<td>Dilution of precision
</td>
<td>[recommended]
</td></tr>
<tr>
<td>
</td>
<td>=E2=80=9CGNSSType=E2=80=9D
</td>
<td>the information about the used GNSS System
</td>
<td>[recommended]
</td></tr></tbody></table>
<p><i><b>Table 1- Event Header</b></i>
</p><p>Where:
</p>
<ul><li><b>=E2=80=9CPROG=E2=80=9D - Event Serial no.</b></li></ul>
<dl><dd>Events shall be identified by a unique incremental counter for each=
 individual vehicle (independently of the Event code). The =E2=80=9CPROG=E2=
=80=9D of first event issued by an OBU is set at =E2=80=9C1=E2=80=9D. Then =
the =E2=80=9CPROG=E2=80=9D of each new following events is set at [=E2=80=
=9CPROG=E2=80=9D number from previous event +1] even if the OBU is switched=
 off or restarted.</dd></dl>
<ul><li><b>=E2=80=9CTYPE=E2=80=9D =E2=80=93 Event Type</b></li></ul>
<dl><dd>The field =E2=80=9CTYPE=E2=80=9D shall be filled using the followin=
g string, it defines the structure of additional data to be sent with the e=
vent:
<ul><li>=E2=80=9CHEADER_ONLY=E2=80=9D (if no additional data are defined)</=
li>
<li>=E2=80=9CEVENT_ON=E2=80=9D</li>
<li>=E2=80=9CEVENT_OFF=E2=80=9D</li>
<li>=E2=80=9CJOURNEY=E2=80=9D</li>
<li>=E2=80=9CTRACKING=E2=80=9D</li></ul></dd></dl>
<ul><li><b>=E2=80=9CEVTDATE=E2=80=9D / =E2=80=9CTRSDATE=E2=80=9D / =E2=80=
=9CSRVDATE=E2=80=9D / =E2=80=9CSENDDATE=E2=80=9D&nbsp; - DateTime</b></li><=
/ul>
<dl><dd>The =E2=80=9CEVTDATE=E2=80=9D / =E2=80=9CTRSDATE=E2=80=9D / =E2=80=
=9CSRVDATE=E2=80=9D / =E2=80=9CSENDDATE=E2=80=9D&nbsp; timestamps are defin=
ed as UTC time.</dd>
<dd>The value shall be the UNIX format of the event date time (GNSS time is=
 recommended).</dd>
<dd>The logical sequence of such DateTime correspond to following diagram: =
 <br></dd></dl>
<p><span typeof=3D"mw:File"><span><img src=3D"https://wiki.itxpt.org/w/imag=
es/thumb/b/b8/S03P01-DateTime_seq.png/400px-S03P01-DateTime_seq.png" decodi=
ng=3D"async" width=3D"400" height=3D"475" class=3D"mw-file-element"></span>=
</span>
</p><p><i><b>Figure 2- DateTime sequence diagram</b></i>
</p>
<ul><li><b>=E2=80=9CGPSInfo=E2=80=9D</b></li></ul>
<dl><dd>GNSS coordinates and related data provided by the internal GNSS rec=
eiver of the OBU. =E2=80=9CGNSSType=E2=80=9D is the information about the u=
sed GNSS System among following GPS, GLONASS GALILEO, BEIDOU, IRNSS, Other,=
 DEADRECKONING, MixedGNSSTypes.</dd></dl>
<h3><span class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"4.2_TiGR_Events_Coding_System">4.2 Ti=
GR Events Coding System</span><span class=3D"mw-editsection"><span class=3D=
"mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href=3D"https://wiki.itxpt.org/w/index.=
php?title=3DS03P01-_TiGR_-_v3.0.3&amp;veaction=3Dedit&amp;section=3D6" titl=
e=3D"Edit section: 4.2 TiGR Events Coding System" class=3D"mw-editsection-v=
isualeditor"><span>edit</span></a><span class=3D"mw-editsection-divider"> |=
 </span><a href=3D"https://wiki.itxpt.org/w/index.php?title=3DS03P01-_TiGR_=
-_v3.0.3&amp;action=3Dedit&amp;section=3D6" title=3D"Edit section's source =
code: 4.2 TiGR Events Coding System"><span>edit source</span></a><span clas=
s=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></h3>
<p>The Event codes consist of 4 alphanumeric.
</p>
<ul><li>The 1<sup>st</sup> character identifies the type of the Event:
<ul><li>E =3D ordinary exploitation event</li>
<li>D =3D abnormal exploitation event</li>
<li>F =3D Vehicle or ITS Failure</li>
<li>M =3D Maintenance warning (fluid levels, filters clogged, etc.)</li></u=
l></li></ul>
<ul><li>The 2<sup>nd</sup> and 3<sup>rd</sup> characters identify the vehic=
le or ITS Function interested.</li>
<li>The 4<sup>th</sup> character is used to differentiate events related to=
 the same Function, normally to differentiate alerts (orange) and alarms (r=
ed). In some cases, additional codes are used if there are several alerts a=
nd alarms for a similar code.</li></ul>
<p>The List is subject to extensions or modifications according to Telediag=
nostic service requirements and/or Third party new features implementations=
.
</p>
<h3><span class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"4.3_Fault_Event">4.3 Fault Event</spa=
n><span class=3D"mw-editsection"><span class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">[</=
span><a href=3D"https://wiki.itxpt.org/w/index.php?title=3DS03P01-_TiGR_-_v=
3.0.3&amp;veaction=3Dedit&amp;section=3D7" title=3D"Edit section: 4.3 Fault=
 Event" class=3D"mw-editsection-visualeditor"><span>edit</span></a><span cl=
ass=3D"mw-editsection-divider"> | </span><a href=3D"https://wiki.itxpt.org/=
w/index.php?title=3DS03P01-_TiGR_-_v3.0.3&amp;action=3Dedit&amp;section=3D7=
" title=3D"Edit section's source code: 4.3 Fault Event"><span>edit source</=
span></a><span class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></h3>
<figure class=3D"mw-halign-left" typeof=3D"mw:File/Frameless"><span title=
=3D"Mandatory"><img alt=3D"Mandatory" src=3D"https://wiki.itxpt.org/w/image=
s/e/e3/Mandatory.png" decoding=3D"async" width=3D"35" height=3D"33" class=
=3D"mw-file-element"></span><figcaption>Mandatory</figcaption></figure><p>A=
 TiGR Event code is used for reporting fault code status.
</p><ul><li>A TiGR Event code with TYPE =E2=80=9CEVENT_ON=E2=80=9D shall be=
 issued every time a fault code is active.</li></ul>
<dl><dd>As EVENT_ON type, the fault ON event shall comply with standard for=
mat of structure "Header" + "EvtON" + =E2=80=9CExtra=E2=80=9D as defined in=
 12.2 below.</dd></dl>
<ul><li>Same TiGR Event code with TYPE =E2=80=9CEVENT_OFF=E2=80=9D shall be=
 issued when the pending monitored fault code is terminated.</li></ul>
<dl><dd>As EVENT_OFF type, the fault OFF event shall comply with standard f=
ormat of structure "Header" + "EvtOFF" as defined in 12.2 below.</dd></dl>
