<h3><span class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"5.0_Vehicle_mode">5.0 Vehicle mode</s=
pan><span class=3D"mw-editsection"><span class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">[=
</span><a href=3D"https://wiki.itxpt.org/w/index.php?title=3DS03P01-_TiGR_-=
_v3.0.3&amp;veaction=3Dedit&amp;section=3D9" title=3D"Edit section: 5.0 Veh=
icle mode" class=3D"mw-editsection-visualeditor"><span>edit</span></a><span=
 class=3D"mw-editsection-divider"> | </span><a href=3D"https://wiki.itxpt.o=
rg/w/index.php?title=3DS03P01-_TiGR_-_v3.0.3&amp;action=3Dedit&amp;section=
=3D9" title=3D"Edit section's source code: 5.0 Vehicle mode"><span>edit sou=
rce</span></a><span class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></h3>
<p>The vehicle mode corresponds to the VHM field in the TiGR data structure=
s Tracking, event ON and event OFF. It refers to the following status for e=
lectric and hydrogen vehicles&nbsp;:
</p>
<ul><li><b>Standby mode</b> =3D the vehicle is parked and saving battery ch=
arge (i.e. equivalent of "ignition off" for thermal vehicle")</li>
<li><b>Driving Mode</b> =3D the vehicle is ready to drive (i.e. equivalent =
of "engine on" for thermal vehicle)</li>
<li><b>Charging Mode</b> =3D the vehicle is connected to a charger</li></ul=
>
<p><u>Note 1</u>: The charger connection status is detailed in CHS field
</p>
