</span></a><span class=3D"mw-editsection-divider"> | </span><a href=3D"http=
s://wiki.itxpt.org/w/index.php?title=3DS03P01-_TiGR_-_v3.0.3&amp;action=3De=
dit&amp;section=3D20" title=3D"Edit section's source code: 6.3 Vehicle faul=
t event specific context data"><span>edit source</span></a><span class=3D"m=
w-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></h3>
<p>The following context data are associated to each Vehicle fault event.
</p><p>This section applies to either vehicles pre-equipped with VehMan =E2=
=80=9Cnative solutions=E2=80=9D or FMS based applications.
</p><p>Additional context data may be provided on request.
</p>
<h4><span class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"6.3.1_Fault_ON_event_specific_context=
_data">6.3.1 Fault ON event specific context data</span><span class=3D"mw-e=
ditsection"><span class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href=3D"https=
://wiki.itxpt.org/w/index.php?title=3DS03P01-_TiGR_-_v3.0.3&amp;veaction=3D=
edit&amp;section=3D21" title=3D"Edit section: 6.3.1 Fault ON event specific=
 context data" class=3D"mw-editsection-visualeditor"><span>edit</span></a><=
span class=3D"mw-editsection-divider"> | </span><a href=3D"https://wiki.itx=
pt.org/w/index.php?title=3DS03P01-_TiGR_-_v3.0.3&amp;action=3Dedit&amp;sect=
ion=3D21" title=3D"Edit section's source code: 6.3.1 Fault ON event specifi=
c context data"><span>edit source</span></a><span class=3D"mw-editsection-b=
racket">]</span></span></h4>
<p>For each vehicle fault event, a vehicle fault ON event is issued when th=
e fault occurs.
</p><p>If the first state of a vehicle fault is =E2=80=9Con=E2=80=9D after =
an Ignition ON event - code EC10, then vehicle fault ON shall be issued.
</p><p><span typeof=3D"mw:File"><a href=3D"https://wiki.itxpt.org/docs/File=
:S03P01-Permanent_fault.png" class=3D"mw-file-description"><img src=3D"http=
s://wiki.itxpt.org/w/images/thumb/7/7a/S03P01-Permanent_fault.png/400px-S03=
P01-Permanent_fault.png" decoding=3D"async" width=3D"400" height=3D"245" cl=
ass=3D"mw-file-element"></a></span>
</p><p><i><b>Figure 6- permanent fault sequence diagram</b></i>
</p><p>As EVENT_ON type, the vehicle fault ON event shall comply with stand=
ard format of structure "Header" + "EvtON" + =E2=80=9CExtra=E2=80=9D (optio=
nal) as defined in 12.2 below.
</p><p>The list of context data to be provided for each Fault ON event is t=
he following:
