<p><i><b>Table 7- Fault ON event</b></i>
</p><p><u>Note</u>: =E2=80=9CVB=E2=80=9D format is volt*10
</p>
<h4><span class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"6.3.2_Fault_OFF_event_specific_contex=
t_data">6.3.2 Fault OFF event specific context data</span><span class=3D"mw=
-editsection"><span class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href=3D"htt=
ps://wiki.itxpt.org/w/index.php?title=3DS03P01-_TiGR_-_v3.0.3&amp;veaction=
=3Dedit&amp;section=3D22" title=3D"Edit section: 6.3.2 Fault OFF event spec=
ific context data" class=3D"mw-editsection-visualeditor"><span>edit</span><=
/a><span class=3D"mw-editsection-divider"> | </span><a href=3D"https://wiki=
.itxpt.org/w/index.php?title=3DS03P01-_TiGR_-_v3.0.3&amp;action=3Dedit&amp;=
section=3D22" title=3D"Edit section's source code: 6.3.2 Fault OFF event sp=
ecific context data"><span>edit source</span></a><span class=3D"mw-editsect=
ion-bracket">]</span></span></h4>
<p>For each vehicle fault event, a vehicle fault OFF event is issued when t=
he fault terminates.
</p><p>If a vehicle fault is pending when an Ignition OFF event occurs - co=
de EC11 (i.e. vehicle fault ON occurred without fault OFF), then a vehicle =
fault OFF event is issued not later than 30 minutes after the Ignition OFF =
event - code EC11.
</p><p><span typeof=3D"mw:File"><a href=3D"https://wiki.itxpt.org/docs/File=
:S03P01-Pending_Fault.png" class=3D"mw-file-description"><img src=3D"https:=
//wiki.itxpt.org/w/images/thumb/a/ae/S03P01-Pending_Fault.png/400px-S03P01-=
Pending_Fault.png" decoding=3D"async" width=3D"400" height=3D"230" class=3D=
"mw-file-element"></a></span>
</p><p><i><b>Figure 7- pending fault sequence diagram</b></i>
</p><p>As EVENT_OFF type, the vehicle fault OFF event shall comply with sta=
ndard format of structure "Header" + "EvtOFF" as defined in 12.2 below.
</p><p>The list of context data to be provided for each Fault OFF event is =
the following:
</p>
