<h2><span class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"7_ITS_fault_events">7 ITS fault event=
s</span><span class=3D"mw-editsection"><span class=3D"mw-editsection-bracke=
t">[</span><a href=3D"https://wiki.itxpt.org/w/index.php?title=3DS03P01-_Ti=
GR_-_v3.0.3&amp;veaction=3Dedit&amp;section=3D24" title=3D"Edit section: 7 =
ITS fault events" class=3D"mw-editsection-visualeditor"><span>edit</span></=
a><span class=3D"mw-editsection-divider"> | </span><a href=3D"https://wiki.=
itxpt.org/w/index.php?title=3DS03P01-_TiGR_-_v3.0.3&amp;action=3Dedit&amp;s=
ection=3D24" title=3D"Edit section's source code: 7 ITS fault events"><span=
>edit source</span></a><span class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></spa=
n></h2>
<p>An ITS fault consists of failure =E2=80=9CF=E2=80=9D code or maintenance=
 warning =E2=80=9CM=E2=80=9D code for ITS modules like AVMS, ticketing, pas=
senger information, video surveillance, passenger counting=E2=80=A6
</p><p>The list of faults for ITS modules supported by Telediagnostic serve=
r is defined between the FM supplier and Telediagnostic service supplier.
</p><p>Onboard ITS modules report their error state using DNS-SD and the ke=
y's "status" and/or "xstatus" as defined in S02-P01 Inventory service. The =
transcodification of S02-P01 error state into TiGR Event codes shall be bas=
ed on =E2=80=9Ctranslation tables=E2=80=9D implemented in the ITS web servi=
ce Client.=20
</p><p>The following context data are associated to each ITS fault event.=
=20
</p><p>Additional context data may be provided on request.
</p>
<h3><span class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"7.1_ITS_Fault_ON_event_specific_conte=
xt_data">7.1 ITS Fault ON event specific context data</span><span class=3D"=
mw-editsection"><span class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href=3D"h=
ttps://wiki.itxpt.org/w/index.php?title=3DS03P01-_TiGR_-_v3.0.3&amp;veactio=
n=3Dedit&amp;section=3D25" title=3D"Edit section: 7.1 ITS Fault ON event sp=
ecific context data" class=3D"mw-editsection-visualeditor"><span>edit</span=
></a><span class=3D"mw-editsection-divider"> | </span><a href=3D"https://wi=
ki.itxpt.org/w/index.php?title=3DS03P01-_TiGR_-_v3.0.3&amp;action=3Dedit&am=
p;section=3D25" title=3D"Edit section's source code: 7.1 ITS Fault ON event=
 specific context data"><span>edit source</span></a><span class=3D"mw-edits=
ection-bracket">]</span></span></h3>
<p>For each ITS fault event, an ITS fault ON event is issued when the fault=
 occurs.
</p><p>As EVENT_ON type, the ITS fault ON event shall comply with standard =
format of structure "Header" + "EvtON" + =E2=80=9CExtra=E2=80=9D (optional)=
 as defined in 12.2 below.
</p><p>For ITS fault ON event, only the following subset of context data sh=
ould be provided:
</p>
<table class=3D"wikitable" style=3D"background-color:white;" cellpadding=3D=
"5">
<tbody><tr>
<th colspan=3D"3"><b>ITS EventON context data</b>
</th></tr>
<tr>
<th><b>Field</b>
</th>
<th><b>Description</b>
</th>
<th><b>Availability</b>
</th></tr>

<tr>
<td>=E2=80=9CTCA=E2=80=9D
</td>
<td>Time elapsed from Ignition ON
</td>
<td>[recommended]
</td></tr>

<tr>
<td>=E2=80=9CVB=E2=80=9D
</td>
<td>Battery voltage
</td>
<td>[recommended]
</td></tr>

<tr>
<td>=E2=80=9CSMX=E2=80=9D
</td>
<td>Current vehicle speed
</td>
<td>[recommended]
</td></tr>

<tr>
<td>=E2=80=9CSTP=E2=80=9D
</td>
<td>Doors status
</td>
<td>[recommended]
</td></tr>

<tr>
<td>
</td>
<td>Extended =E2=80=9CEXTRA=E2=80=9D fields (see 7.3)
</td>
<td>[recommended if applicable]
</td></tr></tbody></table>
<p><b>Table 10- ITS Fault ON context data</b>
</p>
<h3><span class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"7.2_ITS_Fault_OFF_event_specific_cont=
ext_data">7.2 ITS Fault OFF event specific context data</span><span class=
=3D"mw-editsection"><span class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href=
=3D"https://wiki.itxpt.org/w/index.php?title=3DS03P01-_TiGR_-_v3.0.3&amp;ve=
action=3Dedit&amp;section=3D26" title=3D"Edit section: 7.2 ITS Fault OFF ev=
ent specific context data" class=3D"mw-editsection-visualeditor"><span>edit=
</span></a><span class=3D"mw-editsection-divider"> | </span><a href=3D"http=
s://wiki.itxpt.org/w/index.php?title=3DS03P01-_TiGR_-_v3.0.3&amp;action=3De=
dit&amp;section=3D26" title=3D"Edit section's source code: 7.2 ITS Fault OF=
F event specific context data"><span>edit source</span></a><span class=3D"m=
w-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></h3>
<p>For each ITS fault event, an ITS fault OFF event is issued when the faul=
t terminates.
</p><p>If an ITS fault is pending when an Ignition OFF event occurs - code =
EC11 (i.e. vehicle fault ON occurred without fault OFF), then an ITS fault =
OFF event is issued not later than 30 minutes after the Ignition OFF event =
- code EC11.
</p><p>As EVENT_OFF type, the ITS fault OFF event shall comply with standar=
d format of structure "Header" + "EvtOFF" as defined in 12.2 below.
</p><p>For ITS fault OFF event, only the following subset of context data s=
hall be provided:
</p>
