editsection-bracket">[</span><a href=3D"https://wiki.itxpt.org/w/index.php?=
title=3DS03P01-_TiGR_-_v3.0.3&amp;veaction=3Dedit&amp;section=3D28" title=
=3D"Edit section: 8 System diagnostics events" class=3D"mw-editsection-visu=
aleditor"><span>edit</span></a><span class=3D"mw-editsection-divider"> | </=
span><a href=3D"https://wiki.itxpt.org/w/index.php?title=3DS03P01-_TiGR_-_v=
3.0.3&amp;action=3Dedit&amp;section=3D28" title=3D"Edit section's source co=
de: 8 System diagnostics events"><span>edit source</span></a><span class=3D=
"mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></h2>
<figure class=3D"mw-halign-left" typeof=3D"mw:File/Frameless"><span title=
=3D"Mandatory"><img alt=3D"Mandatory" src=3D"https://wiki.itxpt.org/w/image=
s/e/e3/Mandatory.png" decoding=3D"async" width=3D"35" height=3D"33" class=
=3D"mw-file-element"></span><figcaption>Mandatory</figcaption></figure><p> =
The FM gateway shall report to Telediagnostic server any loss of connection=
, OBU fault or abnormal condition which may have an impact on Telediagnosti=
c service.
</p><p>The transcodification of S02-P01 error state into TiGR Event codes s=
hall be based on =E2=80=9Ctranslation tables=E2=80=9D implemented in the te=
lediagnostic web service Client.=20
</p><p>The following table summarize the fault codes applicable in the diff=
erent situations:
</p>
<table class=3D"wikitable" style=3D"background-color:white;" cellpadding=3D=
"5">
<tbody><tr>
<th><b>Event CODE</b>
</th>
<th><b>Description</b>
</th>
<th><b>Remarks</b>
</th></tr>
<tr>
<td>FIB0
</td>
<td>Connectivity failure
</td>
<td>This alarm shall be generated by the FM gateway in case of abnormal int=
erruption of communications with the OBU. <br>The strategy for the detectin=
g the failure is depending on FM implementation.<br>Transition OFF Events s=
hall be issued only when the connection with the OBU has been reactivated.
</td></tr>

<tr>
<td>FIB1
</td>
<td>Failure of CAN connections to the vehicle
</td>
<td>Applicable to either connections to internal CAN in case of pre-equipme=
nt by the VehMan, or to FMS standard connector in case of FMS based applica=
tions.
</td></tr>

<tr>
<td>FIB2
</td>
<td>On-board RT Clock malfunctions
</td>
<td>This alert is reserved for On-board RT Clock failures (normally detecte=
d by the OBU self-diagnostic system)
</td></tr>

<tr>
<td>FIB3
</td>
<td>GNSS module malfunctions
</td>
<td>This alert is reserved for GNSS failures (normally detected by the OBU =
self-diagnostic system)
</td></tr>

<tr>
<td>FIB4
</td>
<td>Cellular malfunctions
</td>
<td>This alert is reserved for cellular failures (normally detected by the =
OBU self-diagnostic system)
</td></tr>

<tr>
<td>FIB5
</td>
<td>Gyrometer failure
</td>
<td>Where applicable
</td></tr>

<tr>
<td>FIB6
</td>
<td>Wi-Fi module failure
</td>
<td>Where applicable
</td></tr>

<tr>
<td>FIB7
</td>
<td>Unexpected shutdown
</td>
<td>This alert shall be generated by the FM gateway in case of abnormal int=
erruption of permanent power supply with the OBU.<br>If the OBU is not equi=
pped with autonomous battery, this alert is generated at the next ignition =
of the vehicle.
</td></tr>

<tr>
<td>DIB3
</td>
<td>Insufficient GNSS signal
</td>
<td>This alert shall be generated by the OBU to trace the cause of wrong or=
 not accurate coordinates in the Events sent to Telediagnostic
</td></tr>

<tr>
<td>DIB4
</td>
<td>Insufficient cellular signal
</td>
<td>This alert shall be generated by the OBU to trace the cause of delayed =
transmission of Events to Telediagnostic
</td></tr></tbody></table>
<p><b>Table 13- Fault codes</b>
</p>
<h3><span class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"8.1_System_diagnostics_ON_event_speci=
fic_context_data">8.1 System diagnostics ON event specific context data</sp=
an><span class=3D"mw-editsection"><span class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">[<=
/span><a href=3D"https://wiki.itxpt.org/w/index.php?title=3DS03P01-_TiGR_-_=
v3.0.3&amp;veaction=3Dedit&amp;section=3D29" title=3D"Edit section: 8.1 Sys=
tem diagnostics ON event specific context data" class=3D"mw-editsection-vis=
ualeditor"><span>edit</span></a><span class=3D"mw-editsection-divider"> | <=
/span><a href=3D"https://wiki.itxpt.org/w/index.php?title=3DS03P01-_TiGR_-_=
v3.0.3&amp;action=3Dedit&amp;section=3D29" title=3D"Edit section's source c=
ode: 8.1 System diagnostics ON event specific context data"><span>edit sour=
ce</span></a><span class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></h3>
<p>For each system diagnostics event, an system diagnostics ON event is iss=
ued when the fault occurs.
</p><p>As EVENT_ON type, the system diagnostics ON event shall comply with =
standard format of structure "Header" + "EvtON" as defined in 12.2 below.
</p><p>For system diagnostics ON event, only the following subset of contex=
t data should be provided:
</p>
<table class=3D"wikitable" cellpadding=3D"5" style=3D"background-color:whit=
e;">
<tbody><tr>
<th colspan=3D"3"><b>System diagnostics EventON context data</b>
</th></tr>
<tr>
<th><b>Field</b>
</th>
<th><b>Description</b>
</th>
<th><b>Availability</b>
</th></tr>
<tr>
<td>=E2=80=9CTCA=E2=80=9D
</td>
<td>Time elapsed from Ignition ON
</td>
<td>[recommended]
</td></tr>
<tr>
<td>=E2=80=9CVB=E2=80=9D
</td>
<td>Battery voltage (24V network)
</td>
<td>[recommended]
</td></tr>
<tr>
<td>=E2=80=9CSMX=E2=80=9D
</td>
<td>Current vehicle speed
</td>
<td>[recommended]
</td></tr>
<tr>
<td>=E2=80=9CSTP=E2=80=9D
</td>
<td>Doors status
</td>
<td>[recommended]
</td></tr></tbody></table>
<p><b>Table 14- System diagnostics ON context data</b>
</p>
<h3><span class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"8.2_System_diagnostics_OFF_event_spec=
ific_context_data">8.2 System diagnostics OFF event specific context data</=
span><span class=3D"mw-editsection"><span class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">=
[</span><a href=3D"https://wiki.itxpt.org/w/index.php?title=3DS03P01-_TiGR_=
-_v3.0.3&amp;veaction=3Dedit&amp;section=3D30" title=3D"Edit section: 8.2 S=
ystem diagnostics OFF event specific context data" class=3D"mw-editsection-=
visualeditor"><span>edit</span></a><span class=3D"mw-editsection-divider"> =
| </span><a href=3D"https://wiki.itxpt.org/w/index.php?title=3DS03P01-_TiGR=
_-_v3.0.3&amp;action=3Dedit&amp;section=3D30" title=3D"Edit section's sourc=
e code: 8.2 System diagnostics OFF event specific context data"><span>edit =
source</span></a><span class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></h3=
>
<p>For each system diagnostics event, an system diagnostics OFF event is is=
sued when the fault terminates.
</p><p>If an system diagnostics event is pending when an Ignition OFF event=
 occurs - code EC11 (i.e. System diagnostics event ON occurred without even=
t OFF), then an system diagnostics event OFF event is issued not later than=
 30 minutes after the Ignition OFF event - code EC11.
</p><p>As EVENT_OFF type, the system diagnostics OFF event shall comply wit=
h standard format of structure "Header" + "EvtOFF" as defined in 12.2 below=
.
</p><p>For system diagnostics OFF event, only the following subset of conte=
xt data shall be provided:
</p>
<table class=3D"wikitable" cellpadding=3D"5" style=3D"background-color:whit=
e;">
<tbody><tr>
<th colspan=3D"3"><b>System diagnostics EventOFF context data</b>
</th></tr>
<tr>
<th><b>Field</b>
</th>
<th><b>Description</b>
</th>
<th><b>Availability</b>
</th></tr>
<tr>
<td>=E2=80=9CPROGON=E2=80=9D
</td>
<td>=E2=80=9DPROG=E2=80=9D value of related Event ON
</td>
<td>[mandatory]
</td></tr>
<tr>
<td>=E2=80=9CEVD=E2=80=9D
</td>
<td>Fault duration
</td>
<td>[mandatory]
</td></tr>
<tr>
<td>=E2=80=9CFOD=E2=80=9D
</td>
<td>Distance driven while fault pending
</td>
<td>[recommended if applicable]
</td></tr></tbody></table>
