</p>
<h2><span class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"9_Manual_input_events">9 Manual input=
 events</span><span class=3D"mw-editsection"><span class=3D"mw-editsection-=
bracket">[</span><a href=3D"https://wiki.itxpt.org/w/index.php?title=3DS03P=
01-_TiGR_-_v3.0.3&amp;veaction=3Dedit&amp;section=3D31" title=3D"Edit secti=
on: 9 Manual input events" class=3D"mw-editsection-visualeditor"><span>edit=
</span></a><span class=3D"mw-editsection-divider"> | </span><a href=3D"http=
s://wiki.itxpt.org/w/index.php?title=3DS03P01-_TiGR_-_v3.0.3&amp;action=3De=
dit&amp;section=3D31" title=3D"Edit section's source code: 9 Manual input e=
vents"><span>edit source</span></a><span class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">]=
</span></span></h2>
<p>These are events generated by manual input to report any types of events=
 such as:
</p>
<ul><li>Vehicle body damages</li>
<li>Cleanness</li>
<li>Dysfunctional equipment</li>
<li>Unexpected vehicle behaviour</li>
<li>Vehicle faults (complementary to FMS or VehMan native solutions)</li></=
ul>
<p>These events can be reported by the driver before or during operation, t=
he mechanics, or any people in charge of vehicle maintenance or operation.
</p>
<h2><span class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"10_Real-time_performance">10 Real-tim=
e performance</span><span class=3D"mw-editsection"><span class=3D"mw-editse=
ction-bracket">[</span><a href=3D"https://wiki.itxpt.org/w/index.php?title=
=3DS03P01-_TiGR_-_v3.0.3&amp;veaction=3Dedit&amp;section=3D32" title=3D"Edi=
t section: 10 Real-time performance" class=3D"mw-editsection-visualeditor">=
<span>edit</span></a><span class=3D"mw-editsection-divider"> | </span><a hr=
ef=3D"https://wiki.itxpt.org/w/index.php?title=3DS03P01-_TiGR_-_v3.0.3&amp;=
action=3Dedit&amp;section=3D32" title=3D"Edit section's source code: 10 Rea=
l-time performance"><span>edit source</span></a><span class=3D"mw-editsecti=
on-bracket">]</span></span></h2>
<p>When sufficient data connectivity is available, Events should be deliver=
ed to Telediagnostic server within 30 seconds from physical event detection=
 on-board. If this was not possible because of insufficient data connectivi=
ty or other network/server outages, queued events shall start being deliver=
ed within 30 seconds of a working connection being restored.
</p>
<h2><span class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"11_Traffic_on-the-air">11 Traffic on-=
the-air</span><span class=3D"mw-editsection"><span class=3D"mw-editsection-=
bracket">[</span><a href=3D"https://wiki.itxpt.org/w/index.php?title=3DS03P=
01-_TiGR_-_v3.0.3&amp;veaction=3Dedit&amp;section=3D33" title=3D"Edit secti=
on: 11 Traffic on-the-air" class=3D"mw-editsection-visualeditor"><span>edit=
</span></a><span class=3D"mw-editsection-divider"> | </span><a href=3D"http=
s://wiki.itxpt.org/w/index.php?title=3DS03P01-_TiGR_-_v3.0.3&amp;action=3De=
dit&amp;section=3D33" title=3D"Edit section's source code: 11 Traffic on-th=
e-air"><span>edit source</span></a><span class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">]=
</span></span></h2>
<p>In the event that the back-office connection with the vehicle third part=
y OBU is managed via a cellular network, the third-party system shall imple=
ment intelligent =E2=80=9Ctraffic saving=E2=80=9D strategies to minimize th=
e service extra-costs determined by the monitoring of TTS status.=20
</p>
<h2><span class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"12_Implementation">12 Implementation<=
/span><span class=3D"mw-editsection"><span class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket"=
>[</span><a href=3D"https://wiki.itxpt.org/w/index.php?title=3DS03P01-_TiGR=
_-_v3.0.3&amp;veaction=3Dedit&amp;section=3D34" title=3D"Edit section: 12 I=
mplementation" class=3D"mw-editsection-visualeditor"><span>edit</span></a><=
span class=3D"mw-editsection-divider"> | </span><a href=3D"https://wiki.itx=
pt.org/w/index.php?title=3DS03P01-_TiGR_-_v3.0.3&amp;action=3Dedit&amp;sect=
ion=3D34" title=3D"Edit section's source code: 12 Implementation"><span>edi=
t source</span></a><span class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></=
h2>
<p>A Web Service shall be implemented by the FM third part.
</p><p>The message shall be encapsulated in a Json stream and sent to the T=
elediagnostic Web Service as a HTTP POST request.=20
</p><p><a href=3D"https://wiki.itxpt.org/docs/S02P00-_Networks_and_Protocol=
s" class=3D"mw-redirect" title=3D"S02P00- Networks and Protocols">S02P00-Ne=
tworks and Protocols</a> contains some general recommendations about <a hre=
f=3D"https://wiki.itxpt.org/docs/S02P00-_Networks_and_Protocols#Http_header=
s" class=3D"mw-redirect" title=3D"S02P00- Networks and Protocols">http head=
ers</a> and <a href=3D"https://wiki.itxpt.org/docs/S02P00-_Networks_and_Pro=
tocols#Http_response_codes" class=3D"mw-redirect" title=3D"S02P00- Networks=
 and Protocols">http response codes</a>. When applicable, an implementation=
 should follow these guidelines.=20
</p>
<h3><span class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"12.1_Structures_requirements">12.1 St=
ructures requirements</span><span class=3D"mw-editsection"><span class=3D"m=
w-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href=3D"https://wiki.itxpt.org/w/index.ph=
p?title=3DS03P01-_TiGR_-_v3.0.3&amp;veaction=3Dedit&amp;section=3D35" title=
=3D"Edit section: 12.1 Structures requirements" class=3D"mw-editsection-vis=
ualeditor"><span>edit</span></a><span class=3D"mw-editsection-divider"> | <=
/span><a href=3D"https://wiki.itxpt.org/w/index.php?title=3DS03P01-_TiGR_-_=
v3.0.3&amp;action=3Dedit&amp;section=3D35" title=3D"Edit section's source c=
ode: 12.1 Structures requirements"><span>edit source</span></a><span class=
=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></h3>
<p>All mandatory parameters shall be filled in order to send the message to=
 the Telediagnostic server.=20
</p><p>If a mandatory parameter is not valid or not available on-board, the=
 related field value shall be set to <b>NULL</b> as defined in S02P00.
</p><p>The Telediagnostic server will automatically translate them into =E2=
=80=9CND=E2=80=9D.
</p><p><u>For Header structure:</u> &nbsp;
</p><p>If the GNSS localization is not sufficiently accurate or not availab=
le, all the fields in the structure =E2=80=9CGPSInfo=E2=80=9D shall be sets=
 as <b>0</b>.=20
</p><p>For UNIX formatted parameters (=E2=80=9CEVTDATE=E2=80=9D, =E2=80=9CT=
RSDATE=E2=80=9D, =E2=80=9CSENDDATE=E2=80=9D and =E2=80=9CSRVDATE=E2=80=9D):=
 timestamps shall be provided in UTC as defined in 4.1 Event Header.
</p>
